@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+# Local changes to page-flip 2.0.7
+
+Source: the installed upstream `page-flip@2.0.7` package, MIT license retained in `LICENSE`. This candidate uses the original soft-page geometry, polygon clipping, and shadow renderer. These edits are local; they are not an upstream release.
+
+- Preserve the declared density of an odd final leaf. Explicit `showCover` behavior remains available.
+- Recover failed boundary drags to `read`; serialize settling animations and reject new flips while settling.
+- Add `PageFlip.cancelUserTouch()` for rollback without committing, and route blur, pointer cancellation, touch cancellation, and multi-touch interruption through it.
+- Resolve touch intent after eight pixels, track the initiating touch, preserve vertical movement, and require horizontal-dominant quick swipes. Remove the delayed touch-start timer entirely.
+- Ignore interactive descendants and non-primary mouse buttons when starting page gestures.
+- Make destruction idempotent; remove window listeners, cancel initialization timers and animation frames, discard animation callbacks, and release page collections. `destroy()` retains upstream behavior of removing the engine root.
+
+Acceptance boundaries: controller/lifecycle checks can establish state and cleanup contracts; real Chromium/WebKit interaction and image review remain required to establish visual correctness and mobile behavior.
+
+Local checks (2026-09-08): `node --test vendor/page-flip/engine-regression.test.mjs` passes six behavior tests. The vendored source also passes `tsc --noEmit --target ES2022 --module ESNext --moduleResolution Bundler --skipLibCheck --strict false vendor/page-flip/src/PageFlip.ts`; this uses upstream-compatible null checking, not the application's stricter source policy.
+
+## Application integration
+
+Run `node vendor/page-flip/build.mjs` from the candidate project before dev/build. This uses the existing project esbuild and TypeScript installations; it installs no packages. Import `PageFlip` from `vendor/page-flip/dist/page-flip.js`, and import `vendor/page-flip/dist/page-flip.css` separately. The adjacent generated declaration entry resolves to `dist/types`, keeping upstream null checking local to the vendor build while the application remains strict. Original TypeScript remains unsuppressed and editable under `src`.
